{
  "_doc": [
    "How a literal `options` list reads (SCHEMA.md, `options`), and what a",
    "commit of each text accepts. Authored FROM THE SCHEMA TEXT, not by running",
    "a reader: when this fixture was written the reference accepted the text",
    "`separator` as a committed value, which is the defect it pins.",
    "",
    "rows: one per offered item, in order. An option row is",
    "{kind: option, value: <the declared value, JSON-typed>, label: <string>}",
    "plus `glyph` when the item declares one; a divider row is {kind: separator}.",
    "A bare item's label is its value's text as the reference's str() writes it.",
    "",
    "commits: `parse_commit` on a `select` carrying these options:",
    "{text, accepted, value}; `value` is null when refused."
  ],
  "vectors": [
